      <string id="Cat_Updates">Updates</string>
      <string id="Cat_Limits">What people can do</string>
      <string id="P_Experience">Look</string>
      <string id="E_Experience">Which look the Start menu, search and the settings window use.

Enabled sets it to the value below, and people can't change it. Disabled or Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_Experience">Which look the Start menu, search and the settings window use.

A default people can change: Enabled sets it to the value below until they change it themselves. Disabled or Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="I_Experience_0">Windows 11</string>
      <string id="I_Experience_1">Windows 10</string>
      <string id="I_Experience_2">Windows 7</string>
      <string id="I_Experience_3">Windows XP</string>
      <string id="I_Experience_4">Startline</string>
      <string id="P_Language">Language</string>
      <string id="E_Language">The language Startline shows its text in: system follows the language Windows is shown in when it's English, German or Italian, and uses English otherwise.

Enabled sets it to the value below, and people can't change it. Disabled or Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_Language">The language Startline shows its text in: system follows the language Windows is shown in when it's English, German or Italian, and uses English otherwise.

A default people can change: Enabled sets it to the value below until they change it themselves. Disabled or Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="I_Language_0">The language Windows is shown in</string>
      <string id="I_Language_1">English</string>
      <string id="I_Language_2">Deutsch</string>
      <string id="I_Language_3">Italiano</string>
      <string id="P_TextAndIconSize">Text and icon size</string>
      <string id="E_TextAndIconSize">In percent. The settings window offers 90 (small), 100 (normal) and 115 (large).

Enabled sets it to the value below, and people can't change it. Disabled or Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_TextAndIconSize">In percent. The settings window offers 90 (small), 100 (normal) and 115 (large).

A default people can change: Enabled sets it to the value below until they change it themselves. Disabled or Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_Mica">Mica behind the Start menu</string>
      <string id="E_Mica">Windows 11's Mica material behind the Start menu, tinted by the desktop picture, instead of frosted glass. Windows 11 version 22H2 and later; older Windows ignores it. For the Windows 11 and Startline looks.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_Mica">Windows 11's Mica material behind the Start menu, tinted by the desktop picture, instead of frosted glass. Windows 11 version 22H2 and later; older Windows ignores it. For the Windows 11 and Startline looks.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_MicaLight">Lighter Mica through the search box and the selected item</string>
      <string id="E_MicaLight">With Mica on, lets a lighter shade of it through the search box and the selected item instead of covering them.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_MicaLight">With Mica on, lets a lighter shade of it through the search box and the selected item instead of covering them.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
