A default people can change: Enabled sets it to the value below until they change it themselves. Disabled or Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_Corners">Window corners</string>
      <string id="E_Corners">Only the Startline look uses this.

Enabled sets it to the value below, and people can't change it. Disabled or Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_Corners">Only the Startline look uses this.

A default people can change: Enabled sets it to the value below until they change it themselves. Disabled or Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="I_Corners_0">Round</string>
      <string id="I_Corners_1">Slight</string>
      <string id="I_Corners_2">Square</string>
      <string id="P_FrostedGlass">Frosted glass</string>
      <string id="E_FrostedGlass">Blurs what's behind the menu. Only the Startline look uses this.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_FrostedGlass">Blurs what's behind the menu. Only the Startline look uses this.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_Opacity">How solid the menu is</string>
      <string id="E_Opacity">In percent, from 50 (most see-through) to 100 (solid). Only the Startline look uses this.

Enabled sets it to the value below, and people can't change it. Disabled or Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_Opacity">In percent, from 50 (most see-through) to 100 (solid). Only the Startline look uses this.

A default people can change: Enabled sets it to the value below until they change it themselves. Disabled or Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_Sections">What the Start menu shows</string>
      <string id="E_Sections">One per line, in the order they should appear: Pinned, Recent, Frequent, AllApps. Any left out are hidden.

Enabled sets it to the value below, and people can't change it. Disabled or Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_Sections">One per line, in the order they should appear: Pinned, Recent, Frequent, AllApps. Any left out are hidden.

A default people can change: Enabled sets it to the value below until they change it themselves. Disabled or Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_RecentCount">Number of recent files</string>
      <string id="E_RecentCount">Enabled sets it to the value below, and people can't change it. Disabled or Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_RecentCount">A default people can change: Enabled sets it to the value below until they change it themselves. Disabled or Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_FrequentCount">Number of most-used items</string>
      <string id="E_FrequentCount">Enabled sets it to the value below, and people can't change it. Disabled or Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_FrequentCount">A default people can change: Enabled sets it to the value below until they change it themselves. Disabled or Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchAtBottom">Search bar at the bottom</string>
      <string id="E_SearchAtBottom">Only the Startline look uses this.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchAtBottom">Only the Startline look uses this.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_Columns">Pinned apps per row</string>
      <string id="E_Columns">Only the Startline look uses this.

Enabled sets it to the value below, and people can't change it. Disabled or Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_Columns">Only the Startline look uses this.

A default people can change: Enabled sets it to the value below until they change it themselves. Disabled or Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_TileSize">Pinned app size</string>
      <string id="E_TileSize">Only the Startline look uses this.

Enabled sets it to the value below, and people can't change it. Disabled or Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_TileSize">Only the Startline look uses this.

A default people can change: Enabled sets it to the value below until they change it themselves. Disabled or Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_ShowLabels">Names under pinned apps</string>
      <string id="E_ShowLabels">Only the Startline look uses this.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_ShowLabels">Only the Startline look uses this.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_CompactRows">Compact lists</string>
      <string id="E_CompactRows">Only the Startline look uses this.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_CompactRows">Only the Startline look uses this.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_MediaControls">Now playing</string>
      <string id="E_MediaControls">A small card with what's playing, through Windows' own media controls: the cover, title, artist and app, play or pause, previous and next, and a switch between apps when several play. Works with Spotify, browsers and any player that tells Windows, with no sign-in. Off unless set.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_MediaControls">A small card with what's playing, through Windows' own media controls: the cover, title, artist and app, play or pause, previous and next, and a switch between apps when several play. Works with Spotify, browsers and any player that tells Windows, with no sign-in. Off unless set.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_HorizontalPosition">Where it opens across the screen</string>
      <string id="E_HorizontalPosition">Only the Startline look uses this.

Enabled sets it to the value below, and people can't change it. Disabled or Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_HorizontalPosition">Only the Startline look uses this.

A default people can change: Enabled sets it to the value below until they change it themselves. Disabled or Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="I_HorizontalPosition_0">Left</string>
      <string id="I_HorizontalPosition_1">Center</string>
      <string id="I_HorizontalPosition_2">Right</string>
      <string id="I_HorizontalPosition_3">Beside the Start button</string>
      <string id="P_VerticalPosition">Where it opens up and down the screen</string>
      <string id="E_VerticalPosition">Only the Startline look uses this.

Enabled sets it to the value below, and people can't change it. Disabled or Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_VerticalPosition">Only the Startline look uses this.

A default people can change: Enabled sets it to the value below until they change it themselves. Disabled or Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="I_VerticalPosition_0">Top</string>
      <string id="I_VerticalPosition_1">Middle</string>
      <string id="I_VerticalPosition_2">Bottom</string>
      <string id="P_Margin">Gap from the screen edge</string>
      <string id="E_Margin">Only the Startline look uses this.

Enabled sets it to the value below, and people can't change it. Disabled or Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_Margin">Only the Startline look uses this.

A default people can change: Enabled sets it to the value below until they change it themselves. Disabled or Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_Width">Menu width</string>
      <string id="E_Width">Only the Startline look uses this.

Enabled sets it to the value below, and people can't change it. Disabled or Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_Width">Only the Startline look uses this.

A default people can change: Enabled sets it to the value below until they change it themselves. Disabled or Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_Height">Menu height</string>
      <string id="E_Height">Only the Startline look uses this.

Enabled sets it to the value below, and people can't change it. Disabled or Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_Height">Only the Startline look uses this.

A default people can change: Enabled sets it to the value below until they change it themselves. Disabled or Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_PinnedApps">Pinned apps</string>
      <string id="E_PinnedApps">One per line: Section|Name|Target or Section|Name|Target|Arguments. Target is a file, folder, program or web address, or app:ID for an installed app. Environment variables such as %USERPROFILE% work. As a fixed setting this replaces the person's pins and stops them changing pins; as a default it's the pins they start with.

Enabled sets it to the value below, and people can't change it. Disabled or Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_PinnedApps">One per line: Section|Name|Target or Section|Name|Target|Arguments. Target is a file, folder, program or web address, or app:ID for an installed app. Environment variables such as %USERPROFILE% work. As a fixed setting this replaces the person's pins and stops them changing pins; as a default it's the pins they start with.

A default people can change: Enabled sets it to the value below until they change it themselves. Disabled or Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchFolders">Folders to search</string>
      <string id="E_SearchFolders">One folder or drive per line. Environment variables such as %USERPROFILE% work. This replaces the person's own places.

Enabled sets it to the value below, and people can't change it. Disabled or Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchFolders">One folder or drive per line. Environment variables such as %USERPROFILE% work. This replaces the person's own places.

A default people can change: Enabled sets it to the value below until they change it themselves. Disabled or Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchLocalDrives">Index local drives</string>
      <string id="E_SearchLocalDrives">Names and dates of files and folders on this PC's own drives, read gently and kept up to date as they change.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchLocalDrives">Names and dates of files and folders on this PC's own drives, read gently and kept up to date as they change.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchNetworkDrives">Index network drives</string>
      <string id="E_SearchNetworkDrives">Network drives and shares, including \\server\share places added by hand. Read at most once a day while the PC is idle, one folder at a time, with no watch on the server.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchNetworkDrives">Network drives and shares, including \\server\share places added by hand. Read at most once a day while the PC is idle, one folder at a time, with no watch on the server.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchUsbDrives">Index USB drives</string>
      <string id="E_SearchUsbDrives">USB sticks, disks and memory cards, as they get plugged in.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchUsbDrives">USB sticks, disks and memory cards, as they get plugged in.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchSkipFolders">Folders never found</string>
      <string id="E_SearchSkipFolders">One folder per line, such as %USERPROFILE%\AppData. Everything inside is never found either.

Enabled adds the items below to people's own, and they can't remove them. They can still add more. Disabled or Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchSkipFolders">One folder per line, such as %USERPROFILE%\AppData. Everything inside is never found either.

A default people can change: Enabled sets it to the value below until they change it themselves. Disabled or Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchSkipFolderNames">Folder names never found</string>
      <string id="E_SearchSkipFolderNames">One name per line. A folder with this name is never found, nor anything in it, wherever it is.

Enabled adds the items below to people's own, and they can't remove them. They can still add more. Disabled or Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchSkipFolderNames">One name per line. A folder with this name is never found, nor anything in it, wherever it is.

A default people can change: Enabled sets it to the value below until they change it themselves. Disabled or Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchSkipFileTypes">File types never found</string>
      <string id="E_SearchSkipFileTypes">One per line, such as .iso.

Enabled adds the items below to people's own, and they can't remove them. They can still add more. Disabled or Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchSkipFileTypes">One per line, such as .iso.

A default people can change: Enabled sets it to the value below until they change it themselves. Disabled or Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchSkipPatterns">Paths never found (regular expressions)</string>
      <string id="E_SearchSkipPatterns">One regular expression per line, matched against the whole path whatever the case. A file or folder that matches is never found, nor anything in a folder that matches. For example \\Payroll(\\|$) or \.(key|pem|pfx)$. A pattern that isn't valid is ignored.

Enabled adds the items below to people's own, and they can't remove them. They can still add more. Disabled or Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchSkipPatterns">One regular expression per line, matched against the whole path whatever the case. A file or folder that matches is never found, nor anything in a folder that matches. For example \\Payroll(\\|$) or \.(key|pem|pfx)$. A pattern that isn't valid is ignored.

A default people can change: Enabled sets it to the value below until they change it themselves. Disabled or Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchSkipHidden">Hidden files and folders are never found</string>
      <string id="E_SearchSkipHidden">Things Windows keeps out of sight. Disabled finds them.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchSkipHidden">Things Windows keeps out of sight. Disabled finds them.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchSkipSystem">System files are never found</string>
      <string id="E_SearchSkipSystem">Files and folders Windows marks as part of the system, such as desktop.ini. Disabled finds them.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchSkipSystem">Files and folders Windows marks as part of the system, such as desktop.ini. Disabled finds them.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchResults">Kinds of results</string>
      <string id="E_SearchResults">One per line, first to last: Apps, Settings, Actions, Files, Bookmarks, People, Mail, Web. A kind left out is never shown. Actions are the quick actions: the calculator, clipboard history and sound outputs. Bookmarks also need SearchBookmarks, People and Mail their Microsoft 365 policies.

Enabled sets it to the value below, and people can't change it. Disabled or Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchResults">One per line, first to last: Apps, Settings, Actions, Files, Bookmarks, People, Mail, Web. A kind left out is never shown. Actions are the quick actions: the calculator, clipboard history and sound outputs. Bookmarks also need SearchBookmarks, People and Mail their Microsoft 365 policies.

A default people can change: Enabled sets it to the value below until they change it themselves. Disabled or Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchMaxApps">Most apps shown in the results</string>
      <string id="E_SearchMaxApps">Enabled sets it to the value below, and people can't change it. Disabled or Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchMaxApps">A default people can change: Enabled sets it to the value below until they change it themselves. Disabled or Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchMaxSettings">Most settings shown in the results</string>
      <string id="E_SearchMaxSettings">Enabled sets it to the value below, and people can't change it. Disabled or Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchMaxSettings">A default people can change: Enabled sets it to the value below until they change it themselves. Disabled or Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchMaxFiles">Most files shown in the results</string>
      <string id="E_SearchMaxFiles">Enabled sets it to the value below, and people can't change it. Disabled or Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchMaxFiles">A default people can change: Enabled sets it to the value below until they change it themselves. Disabled or Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchShowFolders">Show the folder under each file</string>
      <string id="E_SearchShowFolders">Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchShowFolders">A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchBestMatch">Best match at the top</string>
      <string id="E_SearchBestMatch">The one result whose name fits what was typed best, whatever its kind, comes first.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchBestMatch">The one result whose name fits what was typed best, whatever its kind, comes first.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchWebUseAddress">Search the web with a fixed address</string>
      <string id="E_SearchWebUseAddress">Enabled, web searches open the web search address. Disabled or not set, they go to the default browser and the search engine set up there.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchWebUseAddress">Enabled, web searches open the web search address. Disabled or not set, they go to the default browser and the search engine set up there.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchWebName">Name of the web search</string>
      <string id="E_SearchWebName">Shown as: Search &lt;name&gt; for ..., when the web search address is used.

Enabled sets it to the value below, and people can't change it. Disabled or Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchWebName">Shown as: Search &lt;name&gt; for ..., when the web search address is used.

A default people can change: Enabled sets it to the value below until they change it themselves. Disabled or Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchWebAddress">Web search address</string>
      <string id="E_SearchWebAddress">Used when SearchWebUseAddress is enabled, and when the default browser isn't one Startline knows how to ask. Must start with http:// or https:// and hold {} where the words go. Anything else is ignored.

Enabled sets it to the value below, and people can't change it. Disabled or Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchWebAddress">Used when SearchWebUseAddress is enabled, and when the default browser isn't one Startline knows how to ask. Must start with http:// or https:// and hold {} where the words go. Anything else is ignored.

A default people can change: Enabled sets it to the value below until they change it themselves. Disabled or Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchChangeWindowsSettings">Change Windows settings from search</string>
      <string id="E_SearchChangeWindowsSettings">Disabled removes every Windows setting search can change.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchChangeWindowsSettings">Disabled removes every Windows setting search can change.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchWindowsSettingsPages">Shortcuts to Windows settings and tools</string>
      <string id="E_SearchWindowsSettingsPages">Disabled removes search's shortcuts to Windows settings pages and tools, and the Control Panel, printer and default program links.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchWindowsSettingsPages">Disabled removes search's shortcuts to Windows settings pages and tools, and the Control Panel, printer and default program links.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchPowerActions">Power actions in search</string>
      <string id="E_SearchPowerActions">Lock, sleep, sign out, switch user, restart and shut down as search results. Restart and shut down ask to be pressed twice. Each can also be removed on its own under Commands people can use.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchPowerActions">Lock, sleep, sign out, switch user, restart and shut down as search results. Restart and shut down ask to be pressed twice. Each can also be removed on its own under Commands people can use.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchCalculator">Calculator in search</string>
      <string id="E_SearchCalculator">Sums, conversions of length, weight, temperature, volume, data sizes and time, and dates such as today + 30 days, worked out on the PC. Enter copies the result. Off unless set.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchCalculator">Sums, conversions of length, weight, temperature, volume, data sizes and time, and dates such as today + 30 days, worked out on the PC. Enter copies the result. Off unless set.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchClipboardHistory">Clipboard history in search</string>
      <string id="E_SearchClipboardHistory">Texts in Windows' clipboard history, found by their words, to paste again. Only while clipboard history is switched on in Windows. Off unless set.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchClipboardHistory">Texts in Windows' clipboard history, found by their words, to paste again. Only while clipboard history is switched on in Windows. Off unless set.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchBookmarks">Bookmarks in search</string>
      <string id="E_SearchBookmarks">The person's own bookmarks, the ones from the Bookmarks policy, and, with BookmarksFromBrowsers, those of the browsers on the PC. Off unless set.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchBookmarks">The person's own bookmarks, the ones from the Bookmarks policy, and, with BookmarksFromBrowsers, those of the browsers on the PC. Off unless set.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_BookmarksFromBrowsers">Bookmarks from the browsers</string>
      <string id="E_BookmarksFromBrowsers">Bookmarks of every profile of Chrome, Edge, Brave, Vivaldi, Opera, Helium and other Chromium browsers, and of Firefox. They're only read, never changed, and open in the browser and profile they come from.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_BookmarksFromBrowsers">Bookmarks of every profile of Chrome, Edge, Brave, Vivaldi, Opera, Helium and other Chromium browsers, and of Firefox. They're only read, never changed, and open in the browser and profile they come from.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_BookmarksLeftOut">Browser profiles left out of bookmarks</string>
      <string id="E_BookmarksLeftOut">One per line, as Browser/profile folder, such as Chrome/Profile 2, Edge/Default or Firefox/default-release. Their bookmarks aren't searched.

Enabled sets it to the value below, and people can't change it. Disabled or Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_BookmarksLeftOut">One per line, as Browser/profile folder, such as Chrome/Profile 2, Edge/Default or Firefox/default-release. Their bookmarks aren't searched.

A default people can change: Enabled sets it to the value below until they change it themselves. Disabled or Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_Bookmarks">Bookmarks</string>
      <string id="E_Bookmarks">One per line: Folder|Name|Target or Folder|Name|Target|Arguments. Target is a web address, a file, a folder or a program; Folder can be empty or hold folders inside folders as Work/Tools. Environment variables such as %USERPROFILE% work. As a fixed setting they're shown to everyone and can't be removed; as a default they're the bookmarks people start with.

Enabled adds the items below to people's own, and they can't remove them. They can still add more. Disabled or Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_Bookmarks">One per line: Folder|Name|Target or Folder|Name|Target|Arguments. Target is a web address, a file, a folder or a program; Folder can be empty or hold folders inside folders as Work/Tools. Environment variables such as %USERPROFILE% work. As a fixed setting they're shown to everyone and can't be removed; as a default they're the bookmarks people start with.

A default people can change: Enabled sets it to the value below until they change it themselves. Disabled or Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchRegex">Treat searches as regular expressions</string>
      <string id="E_SearchRegex">The whole search is one regular expression, matched against names whatever the case. The switch in the search box turns it on and off.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchRegex">The whole search is one regular expression, matched against names whatever the case. The switch in the search box turns it on and off.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchShowRegexSwitch">Regular expression switch in the search box</string>
      <string id="E_SearchShowRegexSwitch">Disabled hides the switch, and searches are then never regular expressions unless SearchRegex is enabled.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchShowRegexSwitch">Disabled hides the switch, and searches are then never regular expressions unless SearchRegex is enabled.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchShowHelp">Help button in the search box</string>
      <string id="E_SearchShowHelp">The ? that shows what can be typed: words, &quot;exact text&quot;, wildcards, -without, ext:, kind:, size:, modified: and regular expressions.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchShowHelp">The ? that shows what can be typed: words, &quot;exact text&quot;, wildcards, -without, ext:, kind:, size:, modified: and regular expressions.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchFileTypeButtons">File type buttons under search</string>
      <string id="E_SearchFileTypeButtons">The buttons that narrow results to one kind of file.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchFileTypeButtons">The buttons that narrow results to one kind of file.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchShowTime">Show how long a search took</string>
      <string id="E_SearchShowTime">Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchShowTime">A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchShowHints">Keyboard hints under the results</string>
      <string id="E_SearchShowHints">The line that says what Enter, Ctrl+Enter, Shift+Enter and Esc do.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchShowHints">The line that says what Enter, Ctrl+Enter, Shift+Enter and Esc do.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_StartWithWindows">Start with Windows</string>
      <string id="E_StartWithWindows">Keeps the Start menu working after a restart.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_StartWithWindows">Keeps the Start menu working after a restart.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_TakeOverStartKey">Start key and button open this menu</string>
      <string id="E_TakeOverStartKey">Shift + Start still opens the Windows menu.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_TakeOverStartKey">Shift + Start still opens the Windows menu.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_TakeOverSearchKey">Start + S opens this menu too</string>
      <string id="E_TakeOverSearchKey">Other Windows shortcuts keep working.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_TakeOverSearchKey">Other Windows shortcuts keep working.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SkipWelcome">Skip the welcome note</string>
      <string id="E_SkipWelcome">Enabled hides the note shown on the first run.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SkipWelcome">Enabled hides the note shown on the first run.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_M365Account">Microsoft 365 account</string>
      <string id="E_M365Account">Lets people sign in with a work or school account, for their calendar and to find people and mail. Disabled, no one can sign in and Startline never contacts Microsoft. Off unless set.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_M365Account">Lets people sign in with a work or school account, for their calendar and to find people and mail. Disabled, no one can sign in and Startline never contacts Microsoft. Off unless set.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_M365Calendar">Calendar beside the menu</string>
      <string id="E_M365Calendar">Today's calendar in a panel beside the menu, in the Windows 11 and Startline looks. Asks for Calendars.ReadWrite. Off unless set.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_M365Calendar">Today's calendar in a panel beside the menu, in the Windows 11 and Startline looks. Asks for Calendars.ReadWrite. Off unless set.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_M365People">People in search</string>
      <string id="E_M365People">Colleagues in search, to chat with in Teams, call or mail. Asks for User.ReadBasic.All. Off unless set.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_M365People">Colleagues in search, to chat with in Teams, call or mail. Asks for User.ReadBasic.All. Off unless set.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_M365Mail">Mail in search</string>
      <string id="E_M365Mail">The person's mail in search, by subject. Asks for Mail.ReadBasic. Off unless set.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_M365Mail">The person's mail in search, by subject. Asks for Mail.ReadBasic. Off unless set.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_M365ClientId">App registration (client ID)</string>
      <string id="E_M365ClientId">The application (client) ID of the organization's own app registration, used instead of the one built into Startline. Must be a GUID; anything else is ignored.

Enabled sets it to the value below, and people can't change it. Disabled or Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_M365ClientId">The application (client) ID of the organization's own app registration, used instead of the one built into Startline. Must be a GUID; anything else is ignored.

A default people can change: Enabled sets it to the value below until they change it themselves. Disabled or Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_M365TenantId">Tenant</string>
      <string id="E_M365TenantId">The tenant ID or domain, such as contoso.onmicrosoft.com. Only accounts of this tenant can sign in. Not set, any work or school account can.

Enabled sets it to the value below, and people can't change it. Disabled or Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_M365TenantId">The tenant ID or domain, such as contoso.onmicrosoft.com. Only accounts of this tenant can sign in. Not set, any work or school account can.

A default people can change: Enabled sets it to the value below until they change it themselves. Disabled or Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_AutomaticUpdates">Install updates automatically</string>
      <string id="E_AutomaticUpdates">Startline installs new versions by itself, restarting while its menu is closed. On an install for the whole PC, the Startline Updater task installs them as SYSTEM within the hour. Disabled leaves updates to the person, or on an install for the whole PC, to the administrator.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_AutomaticUpdates">Startline installs new versions by itself, restarting while its menu is closed. On an install for the whole PC, the Startline Updater task installs them as SYSTEM within the hour. Disabled leaves updates to the person, or on an install for the whole PC, to the administrator.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_CheckForUpdates">Look for updates</string>
      <string id="E_CheckForUpdates">Disabled stops Startline looking for new versions at all, for organizations that deploy them their own way.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchSkipAppData">Never found: App data</string>
      <string id="E_SearchSkipAppData">Settings and caches programs keep in AppData. Enabled never finds them, disabled always finds them.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchSkipAppData">Settings and caches programs keep in AppData. Enabled never finds them, disabled always finds them.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchSkipWindows">Never found: Windows and installed programs</string>
      <string id="E_SearchSkipWindows">Windows, Program Files and other system folders. Enabled never finds them, disabled always finds them.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchSkipWindows">Windows, Program Files and other system folders. Enabled never finds them, disabled always finds them.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchSkipDeveloperFiles">Never found: Developer clutter</string>
      <string id="E_SearchSkipDeveloperFiles">node_modules, .git, build output and similar. Enabled never finds them, disabled always finds them.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchSkipDeveloperFiles">node_modules, .git, build output and similar. Enabled never finds them, disabled always finds them.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchSkipCloudFolders">Never found: Cloud folders</string>
      <string id="E_SearchSkipCloudFolders">OneDrive, Dropbox and Google Drive folders. Enabled never finds them, disabled always finds them.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchSkipCloudFolders">OneDrive, Dropbox and Google Drive folders. Enabled never finds them, disabled always finds them.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchSkipTempFiles">Never found: Temporary and log files</string>
      <string id="E_SearchSkipTempFiles">Leftovers such as .tmp, .log and .bak. Enabled never finds them, disabled always finds them.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchSkipTempFiles">Leftovers such as .tmp, .log and .bak. Enabled never finds them, disabled always finds them.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchSkipProgramParts">Never found: Program parts</string>
      <string id="E_SearchSkipProgramParts">Files you never open yourself, such as .dll and .sys. Enabled never finds them, disabled always finds them.

Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off, and people can't change it. Not configured leaves it to them.</string>
      <string id="R_SearchSkipProgramParts">Files you never open yourself, such as .dll and .sys. Enabled never finds them, disabled always finds them.

A default people can change: Enabled turns this on and Disabled turns it off until they change it themselves. Not configured leaves Startline's own default.</string>
      <string id="P_SearchWindowsSettings">Windows settings search can change</string>
      <string id="E_SearchWindowsSettings">Unticked settings are removed from search.

Enabled applies the ticks below. Disabled or Not configured allows everything.</string>
      <string id="P_Commands">Commands people can use</string>
      <string id="E_Commands">Unticked commands are removed everywhere they appear. Removing Customize Startline also closes off the settings window.

Enabled applies the ticks below. Disabled or Not configured allows everything.</string>
      <string id="P_RightClickOptions">Right-click options</string>
      <string id="E_RightClickOptions">Unticked options are removed. Their keyboard shortcuts stop working too.

Enabled applies the ticks below. Disabled or Not configured allows everything.</string>
    </stringTable>
